	Leveldrain does exactly what it sounds like: it lowers
the character level of the poor hapless victim. A level 9 creature
is only level 8 after one collision with Stormy, and level 7 after
two hits. As a monster's level goes down, his chances of making
a successful attack go down. So beasts even slightly battered by
Stormy are never again as nasty as they were.
	Incidentally, I don't think Nethack has any equivalent
to the player's Strenth characteristic for monsters. Monsters
attack and do damage strictly according to monster type. Only
their chances of actually hitting vary, and those with their
level.
